{"name":"Heart of Palm","hex":"#d2cfa6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heart of palm","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vegetable harvested from the inner core and growing bud of certain palm trees, especially the peach palm (Bactris gasipaes), which is often grown for the purpose."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart_of_palm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heart of palm","blocks":[{"text":"Heart of palm is a vegetable harvested from the inner core and growing bud of certain palm trees, most notably the coconut, juçara, açaí palm, palmetto, and peach palm. Heart of palm may be eaten on its own, and often it is eaten in a salad. Hearts of palm are traditionally harvested in the cultures of Southeast Asia and in South and Central America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Heart_of_palm.jpg/330px-Heart_of_palm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart_of_palm","wikidata":"Q743144"},{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","wikidata":"Q1072"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/9850Foods_Fruits_Baliuag_Bulacan_Philippines_18.jpg/500px-9850Foods_Fruits_Baliuag_B